mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>本课程以理论课授课为主，开设部分PBL讨论课和实验课，加深对理论知识的理解。</p>
<p>一、理论课（72学时） &nbsp;授课的内容分为四大方面的内容，包括神经细胞生物学，神经递质与受体，神经生理功能和神经系统重大疾病的生物学基础。</p>
<p>神经科学概述（2）</p>
<p>神经细胞生物学重点讲授（共12学时）：神经细胞的结构及血脑屏障（2）；神经元的电活动原理（2）；神经细胞信息传递原理及其新技术发展(2)；神经系统发育(4)；神经干细胞及其治疗研究（2）。</p>
<p>神经递质与受体重点讲解（共16学时）：神经递质氨基酸递质（4）；单胺类递质（6）；神经肽（4）；其他递质（2）。</p>
<p>神经生理功能重点介绍（共26学时）：痛觉（2）；特殊感觉功能及其调节机制（4）；神经系统对运动的调节（4）；神经系统对内脏活动的调节（2）；植物神经功能调节药物（2）；脑电活动，睡眠与觉醒的神经机制，癫痫（6）；镇静催眠和抗癫痫药（2）；学习和记忆（2）。</p>
<p>神经系统疾病生物学基础重点介绍（共16学时）： 脑疾病的病理学总论（4）；卒中脑的损伤和修复（2）； 帕金森病（2）； 老年认知障碍（2）；精神障碍及其药物治疗（4）；神经免疫（2）。</p>
<p>二、实验课：共开设5个实验（20学时实验课），均已在现有的实验中心开设。要求结合理论课的授课时间，安排相应的实验课，深化对理论知识的掌握。</p>
<p>1.神经纤维束动作电位电生理实验（4）；2.大脑皮层诱发电位实验（4）；3.&nbsp;痛与药物镇痛实验（动物）（4）；4.痛与针刺镇痛实验（人体）（4）；5.&nbsp;神经病理组织学</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:70.8500pt;">
                <td width=205 valign=center colspan=4 style="width:123.1000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">课程简介（英文）</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course primarily consists of theoretical lectures, supplemented by select PBL discussion sessions and laboratory classes to deepen understanding of theoretical knowledge.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">I. Theoretical Lectures (72 h)</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">The curriculum covers four major areas: neuronal cell biology, neurotransmitters and receptors, neurophysiological functions, and the biological basis of major neurological disorders.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Overview of Neuroscience (2)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neuronal Cell Biology (12 hours total): </span><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neuronal structure and blood-brain barrier (2); </span><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Principles of neuronal electrical activity (2);</span><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Mechanisms of neural signaling and emerging technologies (2); </span><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neurodevelopment (4); </span><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neural stem cells and therapeutic research (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neurotransmitters and Receptors (16 h): Amino acid neurotransmitters (4); Monoamine neurotransmitters (6); Neuropeptides (4); Other neurotransmitters (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Neurophysiological Functions (26 h): Pain perception (2); Special sensory functions and their regulatory mechanisms (4); Nervous system regulation of movement (4); Regulation of visceral activity by the nervous system (2); Drugs modulating autonomic nervous function (2); EEG activity, neural mechanisms of sleep and wakefulness, epilepsy (6); Sedatives, hypnotics, and antiepileptic drugs (2); Learning and memory (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Key Topics in Biological Basis of Nervous System Diseases (16 h): General pathology of brain diseases (4); Stroke-Induced Brain Injury and Repair (2); Parkinson's Disease (2); Geriatric Cognitive Disorders (2); Psychiatric Disorders and Their Pharmacological Treatment (4); Neuroimmunology (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">II. Laboratory Sessions: Five experiments (20 h) are offered, all conducted in existing laboratory facilities. Laboratory sessions must be scheduled in conjunction with theoretical lectures to deepen understanding of theoretical knowledge.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">1. Electrophysiology of Action Potentials in Nerve Fiber Bundles (4); 2. Cortical Evoked Potentials Experiment (4); 3. Pain and Pharmacological Analgesia Experiment (Animal) (4); 4. Pain and Acupuncture Analgesia Experiment (Human) (4); 5. Neuropathological Histology</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
